WEBVTT

00:29:28.680 --> 00:29:31.201
LW: Then it became a huge success,

00:29:31.225 --> 00:29:33.394
way bigger than any
of us could have imagined.

00:29:33.418 --> 00:29:35.132
AG: Well, you're being very modest,

00:29:35.156 --> 00:29:37.194
but can I get you to describe a little bit

00:29:37.218 --> 00:29:39.229
just how successful the book was?

00:29:40.146 --> 00:29:43.090
LW: I'm not sure
how many millions it sold,

00:29:43.114 --> 00:29:46.357
but it was translated
into many, many languages

00:29:46.381 --> 00:29:52.245
and it was the de facto
web-design book for all colleges.

00:29:52.269 --> 00:29:55.274
It was the "it" book.

00:29:55.604 --> 00:29:57.616
AG: From there,
Lynda continued to test out

00:29:57.640 --> 00:29:58.894
new methods of teaching.

00:29:58.918 --> 00:30:02.076
She started selling
instructional videos on VHS tapes.